Please ask me for the name of an object, then ask for its mass in grams, and then ask for its volume in cubic centimeters.

Work out the density by dividing the mass by the volume, and round it to 2 decimal places. Tell me the density, and tell me whether the object floats or sinks in water. It floats if the density is less than 1, otherwise it sinks.

After that, please ask me if there is another object. If I say yes, do it all again. If I say no, please stop.
